# MCP Server — Cursor Rules

This is an MCP-native server built with Next.js + TypeScript. All integrations are managed through n8n workflows; the app triggers n8n webhooks and falls back to demo mode when n8n is not configured.

## Architecture
- `src/mcp/server.ts` — MCP stdio server entry point. Add new tools here first.
- `src/lib/agent/` — AI agent logic (streaming, analysis, scoring)
- `src/lib/n8n/` — n8n webhook client. All CRM calls go through here.
- `src/lib/integrations/` — Thin wrappers around n8n client with demo fallback
- `src/lib/demo/` — Rich mock data for zero-config demo mode
- `src/app/api/` — REST + SSE endpoints that wrap MCP tools
- `n8n/workflows/` — Pre-built workflow JSON templates

## Adding a New Integration
1. Create n8n workflow JSON in `n8n/workflows/<name>.json`
2. Add typed wrapper in `src/lib/n8n/client.ts`
3. Update integration wrapper in `src/lib/integrations/<name>.ts`
4. Ensure demo fallback when `N8N_WEBHOOK_URL` is unset

## Adding a New Tool
1. Add tool schema to `TOOLS` array in `src/mcp/server.ts`
2. Add handler branch in `handleToolCall()`
3. Delegate to the real module in `src/lib/` (don't put business logic in the server)
4. Return JSON-serialized result with `isError: false`
5. Add test in `src/lib/__tests__/` or `src/mcp/__tests__/`

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode
- Zod for all runtime validation
- Jest for testing
- Tailwind for UI
- Framer Motion for animations

## Demo Mode
All tools must work without API keys or n8n. Use `src/lib/demo/` data when env vars are empty.

## MCP Transport
- Stdio: `npx ts-node src/mcp/server.ts`

## Cron Jobs
Scheduled jobs are handled by Hermes Agent, not the app. See `.claude/skills/mcp-sales-agent/cron/` for skill definitions.
- SSE: `npm run dev` then hit `/api/mcp/sse` (add this endpoint if missing)
